HST Office: closing a document over UNO (Linux, gtk3) crashed the office in ImplBorderWindow::Resize.

ImplBorderWindow::dispose resets the border view and then disposes the ribbon banner (hst-banner-always-visible.patch),
whose dispose joins the banner workers with the SolarMutex released. Meanwhile the main thread ran a posted user
event that resized the border window: SIGSEGV on the null border view (gdb, check-nd30-insertion-point.py under CPU
load: UNO thread SwXTextDocument::close -> ... -> ImplBorderWindow::dispose -> HstRibbonBanner::dispose ->
SolarMutex::doAcquire; main thread ImplHandleUserEvent -> ImplBorderWindow::Resize). Resize would also have created a
new banner on the dying window. A border window that is being disposed now ignores Resize.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

--- a/vcl/source/window/brdwin.cxx
+++ b/vcl/source/window/brdwin.cxx
@@ -1701,6 +1701,12 @@
 
 void ImplBorderWindow::Resize()
 {
+    // HST: dispose() resets the border view first and then disposes the ribbon banner, whose workers are joined
+    // with the SolarMutex released; the main thread may then run a posted event that resizes this window
+    // (null border view; a new banner would be created on a dying window). Nothing to lay out once disposing.
+    if (isDisposed())
+        return;
+
     Size aSize = GetOutputSizePixel();
 
     vcl::Window* pClientWindow = ImplGetClientWindow();
